From 7e75cdb2f56ad20099043a4d91220e3041bb5fc2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domingo Alvarez Duarte <mingo@Domingos-MacBook-Air.local>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:43:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] chore(generate): report generation timings through the
 `log` crate

Stage and lexer timings were behind ad-hoc environment variables
(`TS_DEBUG_TIMING`, `TS_DEBUG_CONFLICTS`) that duplicated something the
CLI already has: `generate --log` turns on debug logging, which is the
same channel the rest of the generator writes to. Route the timings
there instead, so they are one flag away, and so a library caller that
installs a logger gets them without knowing about the variables.

The thread count of the conflict matrix moves into `pair_workers`, which
the `token_conflicts` stage now reports together with the token count, so
the stage line says how the work was split.

The parse-state heartbeat held the only remaining unconditional
`eprintln!` in the hot loop: print it when stderr is a terminal (or when
debug logging is on) only. Sending `generate` output to a file should not
add progress lines just because generation got slow.
